    <openEspRadioProvenance>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_HAL_GET_STA_TSF">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 d01bde81d9b3806e37ef1d9ac3b58af4f5b3d91eeef4f44d20e79d6a9f227542; complete hal_get_sta_tsf at 0x2f82c15c, size 0x36. The function snapshots the station TSF through CONTROL bit zero, conditionally reads the low and high words, then clears the snapshot request.</source>
      <source id="S31_MODEM_SYSCON_STRUCT">esp-wifi-sys commit 2585f278d381acc67c529fa730b91739b5461359, c/include/esp32s31/modem/modem_syscon_struct.h, sha256 1d37b7f4748e9b665ed1bf4f25dc85cd20d25fa5ab2726db82766dd0b506f69e</source>
      <source id="S31_MODEM_LPCON_STRUCT">esp-wifi-sys commit 2585f278d381acc67c529fa730b91739b5461359, c/include/esp32s31/modem/modem_lpcon_struct.h, sha256 af916837fb4c4ed8092fba78a844cc656299acfd63764a420c4c4fdac3472453</source>
      <source id="S31_ESP_PACS_SVD">local esp-pacs commit f823dd9de91c0b83c5e8e85cbea4749dbabc4a27, esp32s31/pac/esp32s31.svd</source>
      <source id="S31_REG_BASE">esp-wifi-sys commit 72b97e6fe55307aa92c8c1edf3fdb3f4df816e80, c/include/esp32s31/soc/reg_base.h, sha256 24a0c98ca63b042ed32d42c5566b979d412e04ec7b1b9d305bb7addc12577f9d; names the HP-system 0x205x, LP-system 0x207x and LP-peripheral 0x208x blocks and IEEE802154_REG_BASE in the 0x201x modem/radio window</source>
      <source id="ESP_IDF_25FE69F_S31_PHY_RETENTION">Official ESP-IDF commit 25fe69f946311abdaf9ad56591f25fedbc20ac98. components/esp_phy/esp32s31/phy_init_data.c sha256 03176e75102562df905e7ec342860ddd120443c2bff043f06d66faef4285b217 defines the FECOEX, FEDATA, FECTRL, FEDATA_WIFI, AGC, NRX, BB and BRX retention bases and register counts. components/esp_phy/esp32s31/include/btbb_retention_reg.h sha256 8acdbdff2393e3d4dc15f1a6aedd240afeb95010e50446c9d596a878fc8af7f3 defines the BTAGC/BB_PART_1 base and count.</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_PHY_VALIDATOR_GAPS">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete phy_ant_btrx_cfg, phy_ant_bttx_cfg, phy_ant_wifirx_cfg, phy_ant_wifitx_cfg, phy_bt_gain_offset, phy_chan_filt_set, phy_dig_reg_backup, phy_fe_txrx_reset, phy_fft_scale_force, phy_freq_correct, phy_get_cca, phy_get_cca_cnt, phy_get_noise_floor, phy_get_rssi, phy_read_rf_freq_mem, phy_rx_filter_mode, phy_rx_gain_force, phy_rx_sense_set, phy_set_cca, phy_set_cca_cnt, phy_tx_state_set and phy_wifi_rifs_mode_en bodies. These bodies prove concrete word accesses and observed read/write behavior, but not undocumented hardware field names or reset values.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_START_TX_TONE_STEP_NEW">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_reg.o phy_start_tx_tone_step_new body, size 0xc2.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_XTAL_DUTY_CAL">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_rx_cal.o phy_xtal_duty_cal body, size 0x392.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_DEBUG_REG_CHECK">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_debug.o phy_reg_check body, size 0x3d2. Its fixed loop bounds and block-name strings prove the half-open hardware dump ranges recorded in openEspRadioEvidenceRanges; they do not name individual registers.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_DEBUG_I2C">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_debug.o phy_i2c_check body, size 0x1f6. Its ten calls prove each logical bank name, block ID, selected host and half-open register-index range.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_DEBUG_PBUS">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_debug.o phy_pbus_print body, size 0xf4. Its finite calls and strings associate selector/path pairs with RFRX, RFTX, BB and DCO groups.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBBTBB_BLE_TX_CONFIG_CHECK">_oracles/libbtbb.a sha256 ebd67c6a32081d0fcd143bbb0ed53f962fc587058e20eceb59012beae47528df; complete bt_bb_v2.o ble_tx_config_check body, size 0x1c0. Its loads, masks and pinned field-name strings prove the BLE TX timing fields, including RF_ON_BT_DELAY and PA_ON_BT_DELAY in the canonical FECTRL word at 0x20100870.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBBTBB_BT_CTE_ACCESSORS">_oracles/libbtbb.a sha256 ebd67c6a32081d0fcd143bbb0ed53f962fc587058e20eceb59012beae47528df; bt_cte.o public getter/setter pairs. Matching independent masks provide instruction-exact CTE and BTAGC field geometry; these BT-only registers remain evidence for a separate canonical BT-radio SVD rather than duplicate singleton peripherals in this Wi-Fi-oriented map.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_ISR_REGISTER_DUMP">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o print_isr_regs body, size 0x5a, and pinned register-name strings. It reads WDEV ENABLE/RAW/STATUS at 0x20104c40/44/48, WDEV_INT1 ENABLE/RAW/STATUS at 0x20104c2c/30/34 and WDEVPWR ENABLE/RAW/STATUS at 0x2010d8b4/b8/bc.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_TEST_HAL_CSI">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete test_hal.o esp_test_get_csi_dump_cfg body, size 0x8a, and esp_test_set_csi_dump_cfg body, size 0x22e. The getter independently proves every promoted field. The setter contains a reproducible vendor quirk: cfg[8] gates the BEAMFORMED update, but retained cfg[1] supplies bit 11.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_PP_DEBUG_DIAGNOSTIC_STATISTICS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_debug.o dbg_lmac_diag_statis_dump body, size 0x17c, and its pinned diag0..diag12/diagsel format strings.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_PP_DEBUG_HW_STATISTICS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_debug.o dbg_lmac_hw_statis_dump body, size 0x252, and its pinned hardware-counter format strings.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_INTERRUPT_GET_EVENT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_mac_interrupt_get_event body, size 0x0a.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_INTERRUPT_CLR_EVENT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_mac_interrupt_clr_event body, size 0x0a; writes the supplied event bitmap to the clear register.</source>
