      <source id="ROM_REV0_PHY_CBW_FEATURE_WATCHDOG">Caller-authenticated ESP32-S31 ROM register-access evidence from complete phy_bb_cbw_chan_cfg, phy_vht_support, phy_csidump_force_lltf_cfg, phy_hemu_ru26_good_res, phy_freq_band_reg_set, phy_bbtx_outfilter, phy_bb_wdt_rst_enable, phy_bb_wdt_int_enable, phy_bb_wdt_timeout_clear, phy_bb_wdt_get_status and phy_lltf_mask_en bodies; machine comparison is owned by vendor-code-validator</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_PHY_READ_NOISE_FLOOR">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete phy_read_hw_noisefloor at 0x2f827d72, size 0x1a. It reads 0x2010708c, masks the low twelve bits, subtracts 0x1000, sign-extends and arithmetic-shifts right by two.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_STA_RATE_CONTROL_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, open PHY/MAC, standard psram-code-psram-data profile and nearby FRITZ HE20 peer, 2026-07-30. The generated PAC plus complete ROM/wDev transform read -92 dBm, scan RSSI was -20 dBm and the blob-compatible signed-byte metric was 72. The Rust-owned association selected Dot11Ax schedule 1, rate code 0x19, maximum schedule 13, 16 entries and BF report mode/rate 1/16. WPA2/CCMP, TID0/TID7/TID5 AddBA, a three-subframe TX A-MPDU and DHCP completed; 100/100 ICMP packets completed with 3.692 ms mean RTT and zero driver RX drops or duplicates.</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_PHY_POWER_DETECTOR">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete phy_pwdet_reg_init at 0x2f82634a size 0x5c, phy_pwdet_sar2_init at 0x2f8263a6 size 0x34, phy_en_pwdet at 0x2f8263da size 0x26, phy_tx_pwctrl_bg_init at 0x2f8267f6 size 0x1e, phy_get_fm_sar_dout at 0x2f8264b2 size 0x2a, phy_get_tone_sar_dout_ at 0x2f8266da size 0x40 and phy_txcal_debuge_mode_ at 0x2f8244fe size 0x56</source>
