      <source id="BLOB_LIBPHY_PHY_CHECK_RX_SAT">_oracles/libphy.a sha256 51497819736295c9b33d6775495dade4c6fb39db887edfe095608c670d9ae223; complete phy_rx_cal.o phy_check_rx_sat body, size 0x76, and relocation graph</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_WDEV_APPEND_RX_BLOCKS">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete wDev_AppendRxBlocks at 0x2f838a7e size 0x132, including descriptor rearm/sentinels, live old_tail.next publication, RX_CONTROL bit-0 reload, RX_NEXT_DESCRIPTOR terminal test and RX_DESCRIPTOR_BASE repair</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_HAL_MAC_RX_GATE">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete hal_mac_rx_enable at 0x2f8386c0 size 0x14 and hal_mac_rx_disable at 0x2f8386d4 size 0x12; set and clear RX_CONTROL bit 31</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_HAL_MAC_RX_LAST_DESCRIPTOR">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete hal_mac_rx_get_last_dscr at 0x2f8386a2 size 0x1e; joins RX_LAST_DESCRIPTOR low 20 bits with RX_DESCRIPTOR_HIGH_WINDOW high 12 bits</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_RX_BLOCK_ACK">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_ampdu.o hal_agreement_add_rx_ba size 0x12e, hal_agreement_clr_rx_ba size 0xbe, hal_agreement_del_rx_ba size 0x72, hal_ba_session_store size 0x4e, hal_ba_session_restore size 0x66 and hal_ba_session_restore_by_hw_index size 0x6c. These leaves prove eight reverse-addressed ordinary banks at 0x20104178..0x20104294 with stride 0x24, live-state/load-word pairs, and update bits zero through seven. Complete extra-SoftAP leaves independently prove the shared staging window at 0x20104ea4..0x20104eb8 plus commit/readback bits eight and nine.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_RX_BLOCK_ACK">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_ht.o ampdu_rx_start.constprop.0 size 0x186 and complete ht_recv_action_ba_addba_request containing the ordinary receive-BA activation branch with the ic_add_rx_ba relocation. ht_recv_action_ba_addba_request extracts a four-bit TID and rejects values with bit three set, admitting TIDs 0 through 7. ampdu_rx_start selects min(peer-requested window, g_wifi_menuconfig+0x30) for a nonzero request, or the configured window otherwise. The later ordinary activation passes constant 64 as the sixth ic_add_rx_ba argument; if_hwctrl.o only swaps interface/index before tail-calling complete hal_agreement_add_rx_ba.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_RX_BLOCK_ACK_DIRECT_BANK_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, fully open PHY/MAC, standard psram-code-psram-data profile and FRITZ!Box 7530 FN HE20 channel 1, 2026-07-30. The AP requested TID0 RX BlockAck at starting sequence five and negotiated window sixteen. Immediately after the open driver programmed ordinary bank zero, typed PAC readback at 0x20104274 reported control 0xc0000001, peer dc:15:c8:54:bc:1e, interface zero, window sixteen, current and loaded sequences five, and zero bitmaps. After two independent 500-packet ICMP receive runs, the hardware-maintained current-sequence word advanced first to 491 and then to 992 while the loaded starting sequence remained five. This qualifies the direct-bank geometry, field packing, publication update bit and live-state/load split; it does not qualify the separate extra-SoftAP staging path.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_TX_BLOCK_ACK">_oracles/libpp.a pinned ESP32-S31 archive; complete hal_mac_tx_get_blockack leaf recovered into MIGRATION_TX_AMPDU and moved to driver/esp32s31/wifi/lmac/src/tx_ampdu.rs. Queue register banks descend by 0x7c bytes. No independent HIL qualification yet.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_TX_TRIGGER_FLOW">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o hal_mac_get_txq_in_trig_flow_state size 0x0c and complete lmac.o lmacProcessTxComplete size 0x25c, lmacProcessShortRetryFail size 0x318, lmacProcessLongRetryFail size 0x266 and lmacProcessTBSuccess size 0x52. The HAL getter reads 0x20104cb4 and returns its complete high byte. The completion dispatcher right-shifts that byte by the completed queue index, masks bit zero and retains the resulting per-queue trigger-flow flag. On a zero-retry-count ACK/retry failure, both retry-failure paths use that flag to terminate through lmacProcessTBSuccess instead of scheduling an ordinary contention retry; the success completion path remains lmacProcessTxSuccess.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_CRYPTO">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_crypto.o hal_crypto_clr_key_entry, hal_crypto_set_key_entry, hal_crypto_is_key_valid, hal_crypto_enable and hal_crypto_disable bodies. The active open STA pairwise/group images were first preserved in migration/esp32s31-hybrid-runtime/src/wpa2_s31.rs and now live in driver/esp32s31/wifi/lmac/src/crypto.rs.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_CRYPTO_INIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_crypto.o hal_crypto_init body. It proves five ordered full-word stores at 0x20104800, 0x20104804, 0x20104808, 0x2010480c and 0x20104810 with images 0x00030000, 0x00030000, zero, zero and zero.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_SET_ADDR">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_mac_set_addr body. It proves the four-interface 0x8-byte stride and, per interface, one full low-address store, one full high-address store, then one fresh-read RMW setting bit 16.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_SET_BSSID">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_mac_set_bssid body, size 0x5a. It proves the four-interface 0x8-byte stride and exact ordered transaction: clear high-word bit 31, full-store BSSID bytes 0..3, fresh-read replace high-word bits 15..0 with bytes 4..5, then fresh-read set bit 31.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_ENABLE_MAC">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_enable_mac body, size 0x18. It performs one fresh-read RMW clearing bits 7:4 at 0x20104c00, then stores its full event-mask argument at 0x20104c40. Complete hal_disable_mac independently sets the same four gate bits before clearing interrupt state.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_INIT_PREFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_init body, offsets 0x00..0x3a. It proves the 0x20104de0 REQUEST-bit RMW, READY-bit polling loop, then the ordered interrupt-disable and all-events-clear stores.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_SNIFFER_ENABLE">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_sniffer.o hal_sniffer_enable body. At queue-three word 0x201040e4 it proves seven ordered fresh-read RMWs: set bit 17; clear bits 0, 1, 2, 3 and 8 separately; then clear bits 7 and 9 together.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_SNIFFER_MISC">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_sniffer.o hal_sniffer_set_promis_misc_pkt body, size 0x84. It independently proves the shared 0x201040f4 misc-packet policy register and its mode-dependent fields. The open frontier uses only the separately HIL-qualified bits 15:8 and does not claim the other vendor branches.</source>
      <source id="OPEN_DRIVER_PROMISCUOUS_RX_FRONTIER">open-esp-radio-rs commit 6a2b358b6dc3458d2f49d80ff14d20aa3d6fabab, driver/esp32s31/wifi/lmac/src/init.rs, first source-owned open promiscuous RX frontier; subsequently qualified by the connected ESP32-S31 rev0 scan/STA run recorded as HIL_OPEN_RX_LIVE_APPEND_2026_07_27. It publishes zero at 0x20104cac, executes complete BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_SNIFFER_ENABLE, sets bits 15:8 at 0x201040f4 through one fresh-read RMW, then issues a device fence.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_RXBUF_INIT_PREFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o mac_rxbuf_init body. Its first four RMWs touch 0x20104c68, 0x20104c6c, 0x20104c70 and 0x2010407c. The final store publishes the external wDevCtrl descriptor pointer at 0x20104084 and deliberately remains owned by the RX ring transaction rather than this prefix.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_LAST_RXBUF_INIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o mac_last_rxbuf_init body, size 0xd2. It performs eighteen ordered full-word stores for six three-word entries at 0x20104124..0x20104170, then two separate fresh-read RMWs setting 0x3f00 and 0x007e at 0x20104120, followed by one fresh-read RMW setting bit 27 at 0x20104098.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_TXRX_INIT_PREFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o mac_txrx_init body, direct prefix offsets 0x08..0xd0 before its first external call at 0xd2. It proves eighteen fresh-read RMW edges. The following hal_he_set_mac_delay, hal_he_set_ack_rate and hal_he_set_bbrxhung_time calls are deliberately outside this source entry.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_TXRX_CALLBACKS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_set_mac_delay (size 0x180), hal_he_set_ack_rate (size 0x156), and hal_he_set_bbrxhung_time (size 0x1e), reached from complete hal_mac.o mac_txrx_init with zero arguments for the latter two. g_wifi_osi_funcs layout is independently pinned by esp-wifi-sys commit 72b97e6fe55307aa92c8c1edf3fdb3f4df816e80, esp-wifi-sys-esp32s31/src/include.rs sha256 de6ecd8853cc1925389f89e768a8a865ad58db6025f94a63584096eb8ad5f1dc and c/headers/esp32s31/esp_private/wifi_os_adapter.h sha256 08fb73f76da7e6800c42dbff2fb724dff5205e1c8262e969da0f391be21f1eae: offset 0x04 is _env_is_chip and offset 0x144 is _random. esp-hal branch esp32s31-async-platform commit 07de55443721de6fa32e7fb721f0fa7996e604d3, esp-radio/src/wifi/os_adapter/mod.rs sha256 cf8439e907161228875d852eb1e4cfa45628b62532bfbe4bc8adcebd8c6112ed and esp-radio/src/common_adapter.rs sha256 6e9ef6acc2236d29e7b2ef2ed957eaa878c8f5f767a77ecff19b6711e135ab34 prove the real-chip adapter returns true and sources _random from esp_hal::rng::Rng. The on-chip blob path uses that value modulo 11; the previously transcribed fixed values were the FPGA branch. Diagnostic log calls after hardware writes do not alter MMIO and are omitted.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_TXRX_INIT_SUFFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o mac_txrx_init body, direct suffix offsets 0xee..0x16e after the hal_he_set_mac_delay, hal_he_set_ack_rate and hal_he_set_bbrxhung_time calls. It proves nine fresh-read RMW edges ending with RX_CONTROL walker-disable bit 31 clear.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_INIT_RX_POLICY">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_init offsets 0x56..0x90 and complete hal_mac_rx_set_policy body, size 0xd2. For each of four queues hal_init performs four direct fresh-read RMWs at 0x201040d8 + 4*q, then calls hal_mac_rx_set_policy(q,0,0,0). Queues 0..2 each add five leaf RMWs across filter, BSSID-high and interface-address-high; queue 3 is rejected by the leaf after its four direct RMWs. The complete cold transaction is therefore 31 distinct RMW edges.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_INIT_TAIL">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_init offsets 0xcc..0x12a, complete hal_mac_rx.o hal_mac_set_rxbuf_reload_use_hw_beacon_enable size 0x14, and complete hal_tsf.o hal_timer_update_by_rtc size 0x38. This bounded tail stores interrupt mask 0x19a879e0, repeats the bit-28 set at 0x20104c8c, performs two separate byte RMWs at 0x20104098, sets RX_CONTROL bit 27, then enables RTC timer update and publishes an 18-bit slow-clock calibration. g_wifi_osi_funcs offset 0x148 is independently pinned as _slowclk_cal_get by esp-wifi-sys commit 72b97e6fe55307aa92c8c1edf3fdb3f4df816e80, esp-wifi-sys-esp32s31/src/include.rs sha256 de6ecd8853cc1925389f89e768a8a865ad58db6025f94a63584096eb8ad5f1dc and c/headers/esp32s31/esp_private/wifi_os_adapter.h sha256 08fb73f76da7e6800c42dbff2fb724dff5205e1c8262e969da0f391be21f1eae. esp-hal branch esp32s31-async-platform commit 07de55443721de6fa32e7fb721f0fa7996e604d3, esp-radio/src/wifi/internal.rs sha256 252cfe7cfdcdb104a91596fcbc173af6e07432b907480df746d0599463c6cdc7 and esp-radio/src/wifi/os_adapter/mod.rs sha256 cf8439e907161228875d852eb1e4cfa45628b62532bfbe4bc8adcebd8c6112ed prove that S31 installs this callback and currently returns zero with an explicit TODO rather than reading extra peripheral MMIO.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_INIT_COEX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_init offsets 0x12e..0x190; complete hal_coex.o hal_coex_pti_init size 0x12, hal_set_rx_active_pti size 0x14, hal_set_rx_ack_pti size 0x1a, hal_set_wifi_default_pti size 0x14, hal_set_ofdma_sequence_pti size 0x13a, hal_set_tb_pti size 0xb4, hal_set_beamf_pti size 0x34 and hal_set_beamf_mt_pti size 0x32; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_coex_enable_default_pti size 0x18. These bodies prove seventeen separate cold RMW edges. The OSI callback at offset 0x1a8 is _coex_pti_get in the independently pinned S31 esp-wifi-sys layout. The esp-hal no-coex stub at commit 07de55443721de6fa32e7fb721f0fa7996e604d3 returns zero without initializing its output pointer. hal_init preinitializes its ordinary RX outputs, but hal_set_ofdma_sequence_pti does not initialize twelve stack outputs before reading them; reproducing that disabled-feature path would therefore publish indeterminate data and is deliberately rejected in favor of an explicit platform PTI source.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBCOEX_PTI_TABLE">_oracles/libcoexist.a sha256 4b00fc4258ac3a7bef3ecd6c0f402d38afde9aafe50ceaf07951406cff576276; complete coexist_api.o coex_pti_get tail-calls complete coexist_core.o coex_core_pti_get size 0x1e, which bounds-checks only the output pointer and copies coex_pti_tab[event]. The complete 48-byte coex_pti_tab object in coexist_core.o .dram1.2 gives cold defaults event 1 = 5, event 3 = 7, event 10 = 3 and event 15 = 1. These are the only events queried by complete hal_init and hal_set_ofdma_sequence_pti. Runtime coexistence may mutate the table, so the PAC fields do not hardcode these policy values.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_INIT_PREFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_init offsets 0x00..0x66, complete hal_init_bf size 0xd4, complete hal_he_set_bf_report_rate size 0x7c reached with arguments (1,0x10,0,0), and complete hal_init_tb_tx size 0x1e. This bounded graph stops immediately before the hal_init_tx_pwr call at parent offset 0x6a. It proves twenty-two separate fresh-read RMW edges and a final volatile read at 0x20107128. In particular, parent clears bit 31 and then bits 31:30 at 0x20104c80 separately; hal_init_bf replaces the entire low byte at 0x20104c78 rather than preserving bit zero; and hal_init_tb_tx clears bits 15 and 14 at 0x20104e04 through separate RMWs.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_UL_MU_OMC">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e, complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_set_ul_mu size 0x3a; _oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40, complete ieee80211_he.o wifi_htc_omc_txcb size 0x108 and its pinned format string. The callback extracts HT-Control bit 11 as ul_mu_disable and bit 17 as ul_mu_data_disable. The HAL leaf independently copies those arguments to 0x20104c80 bits 31 and 30 respectively through two fresh-read RMWs.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_TB_DIAGNOSTICS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_get_rx_trigger_cnt size 0x0e, hal_he_get_tb_times_cnt size 0x0e and hal_he_get_tb_qosnull_cnt size 0x0c; complete hal_debug.o get_txtb_sym_num size 0x10, get_txtb_psdu_len size 0x0e, get_txtb_min_subframe size 0x10, get_txtb_time_pe size 0x0c, dbg_read_axtb_diag size 0x102 and esp_test_get_hw_tb_statistics size 0x56. Field semantics and spellings for 0x201044f4..0x20104500 come from the complete debug function's own WDEVAXTBDIAG0..3 format strings and matching instruction-exact shifts/masks.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_BF_CONFIG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_init_bf size 0xd4, hal_he_set_bf_report_rate size 0x7c and hal_he_set_ersu_ack_rate size 0x4e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_rx_misc WDEVBEAMFORMCONF decode at offsets 0x3c0..0x418 and dbg_read_bfr_rate size 0x148 with its QAM16/QPSK/BPSK format strings; and complete trc.o trc_set_bf_report_rate size 0x52. The decoder proves 0x20104c78 bits 0 through 22. The report-rate decoder proves three 9-bit profiles at 0x20104464, high to low as QAM16, QPSK and BPSK; the setter and trc policy prove each profile packs normalized rate bits 4:0, signal mode bits 6:5, DCM bit 7 and ER-SU bit 8. The trc leaf then tail-calls hal_he_set_ersu_ack_rate: its four fresh-read byte RMWs publish 0x80 for argument zero or 0xa0 for nonzero at 0x20104404.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_TEST_BF_SET_FEEDBACK">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete test_hal.o esp_test_bf_set_feedback size 0x182. The zero-enable branch clears 0x20104e00 bit 23. The enabled path sets bit 23, clears bits 22:20, replaces argument fields 13:7 and 6:0, and applies all bounded selector branches zero through sixteen across bits 22:14 plus 0x2010409c bits two and three. This is an instruction-exact test configuration leaf, not evidence that production sounding calls it or that selector numeric meanings are known.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_BF_DEBUG_CONTROL">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_disable_report_cbf size 0x42. A nonzero disable argument clears 0x20104c78 bit 20; zero sets it. The function then reads back and logs that same bit. Together with dbg_read_rx_misc label HE_BEAM_ENA, this proves the compressed-beamforming-report output polarity without creating a new address.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_BFR_AVERAGE_SNR">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o esp_test_get_bfr_avgsnr size 0x86 and its pinned “Average SNR” format string. It reads 0x20105f94 low byte as stream-zero code, treats 0x7f as the special greater-than-or-equal case, and otherwise computes (code + 88.0) * 0.25 dB using the complete function-local float constants.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_TX_SIG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_tx_sig size 0x350 and its pinned HT, VHT, HE, HT20-length and HT40-length format strings. The complete body selects interpretation from per-queue PLCP_FORMAT, then proves all documented shifts/masks at 0x201054e8..0x20105510-q*0x7c and the matching reverse-addressed queue-protection word.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_DUMP_RX_PPDU">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_dump_rx_ppdu size 0xa36, extracted object sha256 2d3eb6f1123aba62387d98864ecfe1ececc507e52f7f8b72a3efaf40cc5042e5. In the HE-SU and HE-extended-range-SU branch at offsets 0x1b0..0x280, instructions at 0x1e6..0x1ec shift the captured HE-SIG-A1 word right by 23 and mask three bits. The pinned format string at section offset 0x1b0 names that value nsts_and_midamble_periodicity.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DEBUG_STATISTICS_CONTROL">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_clr_hw_count size 0x08 and reachable esp_test_clr_hw_statistics size 0x30. The wrapper tail-calls the leaf, which sets 0x20104c00 bit 16, pulses 0x20104308 bit 0 high then low, and clears 0x20104c00 bit 16 using fresh reads before every write.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_RX_DEBUG_COUNTERS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_color_collision size 0x64 and dbg_read_rx_count size 0x21a, including their pinned format strings. The former proves the BSS-color bitmap words at 0x20104040/44 and RX_HE_BSS_COLOR_CONF fields at 0x20104048. The latter proves 39 named RX statistics, their sparse addresses and widths, including signed high-halfword CFO multiplied by 40 and the hang/panic words at 0x20104c64 and 0x20104e18/1c.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_RX_MISC_DEBUG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_rx_misc size 0x42a and its pinned .rodata.dbg_read_rx_misc.str1.4 strings. The instruction-exact loads, shifts and masks decode WDEVRX_ABORT, WDEVDAHI/DALO, WDEVBSSIDHI/LO, WDEVTXRX_TAB, WDEV_HE_BSSID0_CONF, WDEVAXOPTIONS1/2, WDEVRXCTR_BSSIDLIST, WDEVRX_POWER_SAVE_CONF and WDEVBEAMFORMCONF at their exact 0x20104xxx addresses.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_RESPONSE_RATE_DEBUG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_ack_rate and dbg_read_cts_rate, each size 0x11e, including their pinned ACK_TAB0/1, ACK_SCCKTAB, CTS_TAB0/1 and CTS_SCCKTAB strings. Their instruction-exact byte extraction proves six consecutive response-rate words at 0x2010444c..0x20104460 and the named byte lanes.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_WDEV_DELAY_DEBUG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_wdevdelay size 0x5c and its pinned WDEVDELAY/WDEVDELAY1 format strings. It reads 0x20104c58 and 0x20104c54 and extracts bits 20:10 as WDEV_RXCCK_DELAY and WDEV_TXCCK_DELAY respectively.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_RX_STATISTICS_BASELINE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled AX211 HE20 WPA2 AP on channel 11, 2026-07-29. After HE association, WPA2, successful TID0 AddBA window 32 and one complete 30-profile HE matrix round, the typed snapshot observed MPDU 6216, end 6197, data-success 286, FCS 42, power-drop 42, HT-SIG error 8, HE-SIG-A CRC 1, ACK interrupt 25 and RTS interrupt 6. FIFO overflow, buffer full, TKIP, abort and all four hang/panic counters were zero. The color bitmap had bit 25 set, threshold one and timeout 60 seconds. Four subsequent 30-profile matrix rounds remained clean.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE_RX_CONFIGURATION_BASELINE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled AX211 HE20 WPA2 AP on channel 11, 2026-07-29. After HE association, WPA2, TID0 AddBA and one clean 30-profile matrix round, the allocation-free dbg_read_rx_misc snapshot observed MPDU length offset 380, NFRP threshold 8, hardware TXOP, BSR update, TB stop, TRS, UL MU and UL MU data both enabled, HE response ACK enabled, RX frequency-hop time 50, PHY signal delay 20, intra-BSS-color and intra-PPDU power save enabled, and HE beamforming with BFRP time 16, NDP time 113, hardware sequence selector 5. RX power-save itself and all three custom RX types were disabled. Trigger/TB counters and all hang/panic counters remained zero.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE_TB_COUNTER_BASELINE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust open-radio-phy-prelude-hil on ESP32-S31 rev0 against the controlled Linux AX211 HE20 AP, 2026-07-29. After HE association, WPA2/CCMP setup and more than nineteen complete three-profile DCM A-MPDU rounds, two independent ten-second snapshots both reported RX_TRIGGER_COUNT=0, TB_TRANSMISSION_COUNT=0 and TB_QOS_NULL_COUNT=0. WDEVAXTBDIAG0..3 also remained all zero. This proves the typed read path and a no-Trigger baseline; it does not qualify OFDMA because this ordinary AP configuration did not schedule uplink Trigger frames.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE_BSR_TID_LIFECYCLE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust open-radio-phy-prelude-hil on ESP32-S31 rev0 against the controlled Linux AX211 HE20 AP, 2026-07-29. The fully open STA completed HE association, WPA2/CCMP and a TID0 AddBA response with window 32. Applying the complete vendor TID-bitmap edge at the transition to Operational produced two independent snapshots with WDEVTXQBSR_CTRL TID_BITMAP=0x01. Hardware/software BSR values and validity bits remained zero because the AP sent no Trigger frames. Twenty-four complete three-profile DCM A-MPDU rounds reported zero failures, qualifying the TID0 lifecycle write without an HE SU regression; this does not qualify OFDMA scheduling.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE_TB_QUEUE_PUBLICATION_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, fully open PHY/MAC against FRITZ!Box 7530 FN HE20 on channel 6, 2026-07-30. The STA completed WPA2/CCMP and TID0 AddBA window 32, then prepared 32 owned 1472-byte MSDUs using the complete ROM mac_tx_set_tb order. PAC readback before the HE queue doorbell observed logical queue two, TID0, TB_ENA=1, MU-EDCA selector two and enabled timer, contiguous MPLEN links 0 through 31 with first PSDU length 1512 and terminal link 31, plus WDEVTXQBSR_CTRL validity bit two set. The programmed WDEVTXQBSR_SW value was 47104 but its immediate post-validity read was zero; removing a non-oracle fence and reproducing the exact ROM SW(BSR), LW(CONTROL), SW(CONTROL) sequence did not change that result. The following ordinary HE20 MCS9 PPDU received a complete 32-bit BlockAck and sustained roughly 70-77 Mbit/s. RX_TRIGGER_COUNT and TB transmission counters remained zero because this AP emitted no Trigger. This qualifies the queue/link/validity publication and no-SU-regression boundary, but not the BSR read-latch semantics or over-air TB/OFDMA transmission.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_TX_POWER_INIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o hal_init_tx_pwr size 0x50 and hal_get_tx_pwr size 0x1a; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_init_tb_power size 0x1a0, hal_init_imrsp_power size 0x2f8, hal_mac_set_tb_max_pwr size 0x160 including both complete relocation jump tables, and hal_init_tb_ru_power size 0xba. The parent queries rates 0 through 42 in order into 43 adjacent two-byte entries. Its three children publish 56 separate fresh-read RMW edges at 0x20104408..0x20104448. Migration source is the Git parent of promotion commit f233006, migration/esp32s31-hybrid-runtime/src/lmac.rs: it consumed this same exported 86-byte s_phy_get_max_pwr table for open legacy and HT TX but did not reproduce its builder.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_PARTIAL_RU_MAX_POWER">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_api.o esp_wifi_internal_get_partial_ru_max_tx_pwr size 0x68 and esp_wifi_internal_set_partial_ru_max_tx_pwr size 0x62, plus complete ieee80211_ioctl.o wifi_get_partial_ru_max_txpwr_process size 0x38 and wifi_set_partial_ru_max_txpwr_process size 0x1c. The API stores the caller's first byte unchanged in the IOCTL object and the process leaf passes it unchanged to _oracles/libpp.a complete hal_mac_get_tb_max_pwr size 0x126 or hal_mac_set_tb_max_pwr size 0x160. Their relocation-complete jump tables admit raw Trigger RU selectors 0 through 8, 37 through 40, 53, 54 and 61, select one six-bit field at 0x2010443c..0x20104448, and log “the ru_alloc_num is not correct” for every other value.</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_PHY_GET_MAX_PWR">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete phy_get_max_pwr at 0x2f8249fe size 0x54, phy_get_target_pwr at 0x2f824976 size 0x88, phy_rate_to_index at 0x2f82491e size 0x58, phy_wifi_get_target_power at 0x2f8270fa size 0x22 and phy_get_chan_target_power at 0x2f826da4 size 0x98. Each max-power query first sets bit 14 and replaces bits 13:8 with 0x15 at 0x20107428 through separate RMWs, derives two quarter-unit target powers from live PHY calibration/channel state, clamps each to 84, arithmetic-shifts both right by two and writes two signed bytes.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_INIT_SUFFIX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_init offsets 0x7a..0x19e and complete reached hal_he_set_ersu, hal_he_set_ersu_ack_rate, hal_he_set_bcast_ru, hal_he_set_uora_parameter, hal_he_enable_dump_complete_hesigb, hal_vht_enable_bwsignaling_rts, hal_he_clr_multi_bssid and hal_he_set_co_hosted_bss leaves, plus complete hal_mac_tx.o hal_set_tx_min_pwr size 0x1a. It proves 163 writes/RMWs and two guard reads after the debug power traversal. In particular ER-SU ACK bytes are four separate RMWs, feature bits 1 and 0 at 0x20104c88 are separate, the 120-word scratch range is 0x201055f0..0x201057cc, and the parent/clear/co-hosted sequence deliberately repeats multi-BSSID fields.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_SET_DEFAULT_PE">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_set_default_pe body, size 0x14. It replaces only bits 2:0 at 0x20104c80 with its three-bit argument.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_BSR_INIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_bsr_init body, size 0x50, plus complete hal_he_bsr_ctrl and hal_he_get/set_bsr_acihigh_comp_method leaves. It proves eight ordered fresh-read RMW edges: set 0x20104c7c bits 15, 8, 7 and 6; set 0x20104c80 bit 27; clear 0x20104c7c bits 5 and 4; then replace bits 1:0 with one.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_BSR_DEBUG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_bsr_info size 0x268 and dbg_tb_ignore_cca_enable size 0x3c, including their pinned format strings. The first function decodes WDEVTXQBSR_CTRL, eight interleaved hardware/software BSR values, WDEVAXOPTIONS1 and WDEVAXOPTIONS2. The second proves that 0x20104c7c bit 12 set means TB cares about CCA and NAV, while clear means the debug ignore mode.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_BSR_STATUS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_get_hw_txq_bsr size 0x14. It reads 0x20104d74 plus eight times the queue/TID index and returns the low twenty bits.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_TX_SET_TB">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o mac_tx_set_hesig size 0x324, mac_tx_set_tb size 0x146, mac_tx_set_mplen size 0x2c4 and hal_mac_tx_clr_mplen size 0x1aa; complete if_hecfg.o wifi_he_get_hetb_tid_bitmap size 0x46 and its four-byte table [0x01,0x81,0xa1,0xa3]; complete hal_he_common.o hal_he_get_mplen_addr_start and hal_he_get_mplen_addr_end, each size 0x4a, and their tables. mac_tx_set_hesig calls mac_tx_set_tb unless descriptor-state word offset 0x30 bit 16 is set. The setter gates the QoS TID against the configured bitmap, allocates and writes a linked MPDU-length entry for every DMA frame, writes the terminal link index at 0x201054fc-q*0x7c, enables 0x20104dbc+4*q bit eight, constructs WDEVTXQ_CONF1 at 0x20104d68-0x10*q, replaces the low twenty software-BSR bits at 0x20104d78+8*q with its queued-byte accumulator, and finally ORs 1&lt;&lt;q into 0x20104db8. The default configuration value three returns bitmap 0xa1, selecting TIDs 0, 5 and 7. For that non-single-TID policy the allocator ranges are q0 32..63, q1 64..95, q2 0..31 and q3 96..119. The clear leaf walks and frees the software bitmap chain, while its only hardware-visible cleanup clears queue-control TB_ENA.</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_MAC_TX_SET_TB">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete mac_tx_set_hesig at 0x2f8350a8 size 0x1e2, mac_tx_set_tb at 0x2f834f82 size 0x126, mac_tx_set_mplen at 0x2f836b1a size 0x156, hal_he_get_mplen_addr_start at 0x2f836a8e size 0x46, hal_he_get_mplen_addr_end at 0x2f836ad4 size 0x46 and wifi_he_get_hetb_tid_bitmap at 0x2f839386 size 0x28. The ROM independently reproduces the same fixed-address Trigger queue, MU-EDCA, software-BSR, ready-bitmap, MPDU-link and tail writes as the blob. The newer blob adds only allocation diagnostics and a terminal-frame assertion/log around this bounded hardware transaction.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_MU_EDCA_DEBUG">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_muedca_timer size 0x70, dbg_read_txq_conf1 size 0x86 and dbg_read_txq_conf2 size 0x80, including their pinned format strings. They decode four WDEVMUEDCA_TIMER words at 0x20104dbc..0x20104dc8, eight reverse-addressed WDEVTXQ_CONF1 words at 0x20104cf8..0x20104d68 and four reverse-addressed WDEVTXQ_CONF2 words at 0x20104d34..0x20104d64. The strings identify TID, TB enable, MU-EDCA timer select, MPDU-length link address, minimum TX power, three channel-width minimum-MPDU lengths, software RTS/CTS, timer/reset/reached and AIFS fields.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_HE_TID_BITMAP">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_ht.o ht_recv_action_ba_addba_response size 0x24a and ht_recv_action_ba_delba size 0xda call hal_he_set_tid_bitmap and hal_he_clr_tid_bitmap for HE nodes. _oracles/libpp.a complete hal_mac_ctl.o leaves size 0x2a and 0x2e update 0x20104db8 bits 20:13 with the selected TID bit through two reads followed by one write.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_TRIGGER_RX_DIAGNOSTICS">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_ax_diag size 0x466 and its pinned WDEVAXDIAG0..9 format strings. The function reads 0x20104508..0x2010452c and decodes Trigger state, TB APEP length, EOF/pre-FEC padding, matched user RU/MCS/DCM/FEC/AID, common GI/LTF/bandwidth/spatial-reuse fields, TRS and packet counts. Its own warning says the words are not reliable after a following RX frame, so the PAC treats them as a best-effort diagnostic snapshot rather than durable state.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_RX_BA">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_rx_ba size 0x9a and its pinned WDEVTXQBA_BMHI/BMLO/SSC/TID/TAHI/TALO strings. Despite its symbol name, the function walks eight TX BlockAck result banks from 0x20105528 downward with stride 0x7c.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_DUMP_TXQ_TXINFO">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_dump_txq_txinfo size 0x70 and its pinned WDEVTXQ_TXINFO/BA/ACK/ACK_TID/LAST_TX_IS_TB/TB_PACK_SENT string. It reads the queue-information word at 0x20105524-q*0x7c and the upper result fields of 0x20105534-q*0x7c.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_INTERNAL_TXBA">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_internal_txba size 0x66 and its pinned WDEVTXBA bitmap, transmitter-address, fragment, SSN and TID strings. It reads five consecutive words at 0x2010429c..0x201042ac.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_KEY_ENTRY">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_key_entry size 0x1cc and its pinned key-entry strings. The queue selector reads 0x201054d8-q*0x7c bits 22:17 and 24:23, then indexes the ten-word key table at 0x20105800 with stride 0x28 and the validity bitmap at 0x20104814.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_TX_MPLEN">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_tx_mplen size 0x120 and its pinned MPDU_LEN/NEXT strings. It reads 120 consecutive words at 0x201055f0..0x201057cc and extracts bits 13:0 and 20:14.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_OBSS_NARROW_BAND_RU">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_disable_obss_narrow_bw_ru size 0x3e. A nonzero argument writes 0xfffff to 0x20104e9c, sets 0x20104ea0 bits 8:4 through one fresh-read RMW and bit 0 through another; zero writes zero and clears those two groups in the same order. The aggregate disabled/enabled meaning is symbol-exact, while individual bitmap/class meanings remain approximate.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_IEEE80211_PARSE_HEOPR">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_he.o ieee80211_parse_heopr body and pinned format string "(opr)len:%d, Default PE Duration:%d, TXOP RTS Threshold:%d(%d us), ER-SU-Disable:%d". The input points at a complete extension IE: bytes 0..2 are element ID, length and HE Operation extension ID; byte 3 bits 2:0 are passed to hal_he_set_default_pe and byte 5 bit 0 is the raw ER-SU-Disable value passed to hal_he_set_ersu. The complete BSS-color branch treats HE Operation byte six bit seven as disabled, bits 5:0 as color and bit six as partial. A controlled AP advertised raw value 0x99, so disabled is true and the effective color passed to TX is zero rather than 25.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_DBG_READ_TX_POWER">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_debug.o dbg_read_tx_power size 0xcc. The unconditional hal_he_init child queries PHY rates 0 through 25 while skipping rate 4, for 25 discarded two-byte results, then only reads the MAC table and logs. Through ROM_REV0_PHY_GET_MAX_PWR those otherwise diagnostic queries still cause fifty ordered RMWs at 0x20107428.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_ANTENNA_INIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o hal_attenna_init body, size 0x5e. The symbol spelling is preserved from the archive. Its first reverse traversal clears bit 2 at eight words from 0x20105510 down to 0x201051ac with stride 0x7c. Its second reverse traversal clears bit 3, sets bit 5 and clears bit 4 through three separate fresh-read RMWs per word. It finishes with separate bit-2-clear and bit-5-set RMWs at 0x201042b0. Complete hal_mac_rate_autoack_init in the same object is independently verified as a two-byte ret-only no-op.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_MAC_CHANNEL_SWITCH">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40, complete wl_chm.o chm_phy_change_channel.constprop.0; _oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e, complete if_hwctrl.o ic_mac_deinit/ic_mac_init, hal_mac.o hal_mac_deinit/hal_mac_init, hal_pwr.o pwr_hal_select_wifimac_regdma_link and ret-only hal_mac_ctl.o hal_mac_set_csi_cbw. The exact vendor chain is pm_wake_up, ic_mac_deinit, phy_change_channel, hal_mac_set_csi_cbw, ic_mac_init, pm_wake_done. For WIFI_PS_NONE its bounded MMIO tail sets then clears 0x00ff1000 at 0x20104cac and selects REGDMA link four in bits 20:17 of 0x2010d83c.</source>
      <source id="MIGRATION_CHANNEL_SWITCH">Git parent of migration-promotion commit f233006, migration/esp32s31-hybrid-runtime/src/channel_switch.rs and src/radio_hal.rs; exact finite WIFI_PS_NONE MAC stop/idle/restart and REGDMA-link-four transcription. The original archive was deleted after promotion, but this channel-restart leaf was not wired into the live HIL until the open STA timeout investigation.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_REGDMA_LINK4_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs switch_channel_with_mac_restart on ESP32-S31 rev0, psram-code-psram-data profile, 2026-07-29. An exact working vendor pre-auth snapshot read 0x2010d83c=0x080801ff (ACTIVE_LINK=4), while the failing open path read 0x080001ff (ACTIVE_LINK=0). Restoring the complete ic_mac_init link-four tail produced first-attempt Authentication, Association, WPA2 and DHCP at the ordinary 80-quarter-dBm limit; 200/200 ICMP echoes completed with 0 percent loss and 4.539 ms average RTT. The accumulated open TX counters were 211 immediate successes, three recovered ACK retries, zero other failures and zero hardware timeouts.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_RX_POLICY">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac.o hal_mac_rx_set_policy and hal_mac_set_rxq_policy bodies plus if_hwctrl.o ic_set_rx_policy and ic_set_rx_policy_ubssid_check wrappers. The reachable queue-zero policy-five transaction was preserved in migration scan code and is HIL-qualified by the connected open STA path.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_WIFI_RX_POLICY">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_supplicant.o wifi_set_rx_policy parent and jump table. Case five ends with ic_set_rx_policy_ubssid_check(0,false); case six ends with ic_set_rx_policy_ubssid_check(0,true). Register masks, addresses and ordered RMW edges come from the complete libpp HAL leaves.</source>
      <source id="IEEE80211_HT_SIG">IEEE Std 802.11 HT-SIG field layout: HT-SIG1 bit 7 is CBW, with zero selecting 20 MHz and one selecting 40 MHz. This standard semantic is joined only to the instruction-exact descriptor-word1-bit-15 mapping proved by BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_TX.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_MAC_TX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o mac_tx_set_plcp0, hal_mac_tx_config_timeout, hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu, hal_mac_tx_config_edca, hal_mac_txq_enable, hal_mac_txq_disable, hal_mac_get_txq_state, hal_mac_clr_txq_state and hal_mac_get_txq_complete bodies; complete lmac.o lmacProcessTxSuccess; complete trc.o rcUpdateTxDone and rcUpdateAckSnr; complete pp.o ppTxProtoProc and mac_tx_set_pti bodies.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HAL_HE_TX">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete hal_mac_tx.o mac_tx_set_hesig size 0x324, hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu HE branch, mac_tx_set_plcp0/mac_tx_set_plcp1 and mac_tx_set_len, plus complete hal_mac_ctl.o hal_he_get_bss_color, hal_he_set_tx_protection and hal_he_set_htc. This graph proves the two reverse-stride HE SU vector stores, repeated descriptor-count and protection fields, length-control store and HE power-pair selection.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_HE_CONTROL_TX">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_he.o ieee80211_encap_esfbuf_htc size 0x86 and complete ieee80211_output.o ieee80211_set_tx_desc/ieee80211_encap_esfbuf call graph. The HE QoS/TID path sets Frame Control Order bit 15 without reserving or moving four DMA bytes. An explicit pending OMC additionally writes the descriptor HE-Control word at offset 0x3c and sets descriptor-state bit 16; otherwise the software override stays clear for hardware-generated control such as BSR. _oracles/libpp.a complete hal_mac_tx.o hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu forwards those descriptor fields to hal_he_set_htc after mac_tx_set_hesig. Complete pp_he.o ppCalSubFrameLength independently proves the four-byte metadata accounting used by hardware insertion.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_HE_CONTROL_INSERTION_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/bin/wifi_sta.rs wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver and Android shiva HE20/WPA2 AP, captured in /tmp/vendor-he-control-oracle-20260730.log and /tmp/vendor-he-control-oracle-air-20260730.pcapng. The synchronous post-formatter snapshot captured descriptor rate 35, Order set in DMA Frame Control, no four-byte placeholder before CCMP, metadata word one 0x01000000, software HE-Control disabled, and APEP length 0x76. Air frames 11 and 58 carried hardware BSR HE-Control 0x0404320f followed by intact CCMP. Frame 113 independently carried BSR 0x0303004f followed by intact CCMP. Complete _oracles/libpp.a[pp_he.o] ppCalSubFrameLength reads metadata byte seven bit zero from 0x01000000 and adds exactly four to the assembled subframe, while the low fourteen-bit metadata MPDU length remains unchanged. Earlier open frame 3010 in /tmp/open-radio-android-arp-air-20260730.pcapng omitted this metadata bit and corrupted the CCMP boundary; a temporary DMA placeholder restored length but was not vendor-equivalent.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE_CONTROL_METADATA_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs open-radio-phy-prelude-hil on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete open PHY/MAC, standard psram-code-psram-data profile and Android shiva HE20/WPA2 AP on channel 6, captured in /tmp/open-radio-he-control-metadata-ch6-20260730.log and /tmp/open-radio-he-control-metadata-ch6-air-20260730.pcapng. The Rust A-MPDU builder kept CCMP immediately after the 26-byte QoS header, left the low fourteen-bit DMA MPDU length unchanged and set metadata byte seven bit zero. The driver completed WPA2, its first protected ARP on attempt one, immediate static-address network bring-up, and the first HE20 MCS9 aggregate with 32 of 32 MPDUs acknowledged on attempt one. Air frame 843, repeated as frame 78088 after a clean reset, contained Frame Control 0x88c1, QoS 0x0000, hardware BSR HE-Control bytes 4f 00 03 03, then intact CCMP bytes 09 00 00 20 00 00 00 00; tshark decrypted it as the expected ARP request. Eight subsequent ICMP replies likewise carried hardware BSR, decrypted successfully and had no retries or packet loss. This independently hardware-qualifies the vendor-equivalent metadata contract and rules out a software DMA placeholder.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HE_DCM">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete trc.o rcGetDCMMaxRate and he_get_min_subframe_len_dcm bodies plus their RU26, RU52, RU106 and RU242 rate tables. rcGetDCMMaxRate maps the peer receive-constellation bound to BCC DCM MCS0, MCS1 or MCS3. For RU242 the 100-kbit/s rate rows for GI 0.8, 1.6 and 3.2 us are respectively [43,86,0,172,258], [40,81,0,163,244] and [36,73,0,146,219]. he_get_min_subframe_len_dcm combines these tables with ROM global s_ht_ampdu_density_us, whose rev0 default at 0x2f07fc5a is eight microseconds: it computes scaled=(rate_100kbps*density_us)&gt;&gt;3 and minimum_bytes=scaled/10+(scaled%10!=0), then stores the u16 result in the GI-by-MCS density table.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HE_DELIMITER_SPACING">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_he.o ppCalDeliNum size 0xac, ppCalSubFrameLength size 0x3e and ppEmptyDelimiterLength size 0x22; complete trc.o rcUpdateAMPDUParam size 0xde and ordinary/DCM HE minimum-subframe builders; complete hal_mac_tx.o mac_tx_set_hesig size 0x324. rcUpdateAMPDUParam maps the eight negotiated density encodings through integer microseconds [0,1,1,1,2,4,8,16]. ppCalDeliNum selects the GI, HE MCS and DCM-specific minimum complete subframe byte count, stores it at descriptor offset 0x28, and writes ceil((minimum-current)/4) to private DMA metadata byte four when round4(PSDU)+delimiter is shorter. ppCalSubFrameLength adds those four-byte empty delimiters to non-final aggregate accounting; ppEmptyDelimiterLength removes final padding and empty delimiters. mac_tx_set_hesig copies the descriptor offset-0x28 halfword into all three ten-bit queue PROTECTION lanes. The length metadata and PROTECTION value are therefore two outputs of the same rate/density policy and must not be configured independently.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_HE_AMPDU_LIMIT">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_he.o ppCheckTxHEAMPDUlength size 0x258, pp_he.o get_estimated_batime size 0x1a, and trc.o rx11AXRate2AMPDULimit plus rx11AXRate2AMPDULimit_update size 0x136. The checker calls ppCalSubFrameLength for the candidate and rejects or stops accumulation when it exceeds the u16 limit selected by AC profile, GI/LTF and MCS. It halves that limit when descriptor-state word offset 0x30 bit 15 selects DCM. A zero EDCA TXOP copies ROM_REV0_HE_MAX_APEP into the selected profile. For a nonzero TXOP in 32-us units the producer generates three by ten values using duration_us=txop*32-36, estimated BlockAck times [68,44,44,32,32,32,32,32,32,32] us, preambles [31.2,32,40] us, symbol times [13.6,14.4,16] us, RU242 data bits per symbol [117,234,351,468,702,936,1053,1170,1404,1560], a minus-22 service/tail-bit term and final division by eight. The four AC profiles together occupy 120 u32 entries.</source>
      <source id="ROM_REV0_HE_MAX_APEP">_oracles/esp32s31_rev0_rom.elf sha256 a52ad7513deb656a910a5740125f1cce2c7941f11ce57213b7b43aea93d5ab87; complete 120-byte he_max_apep_length object at 0x2f84fd40. Its three GI rows by ten MCS columns are [3700,7400,11100,14800,22500,30000,33600,37600,45000,50000], [3500,7000,10500,14000,21000,28200,31500,35200,42300,47000], and [3200,6400,9600,12800,19000,25200,28700,32000,37800,42000]. Complete BLOB_LIBPP_HE_AMPDU_LIMIT maps both 0.8-us GI selectors to row zero and consumes these values as u16 APEP byte ceilings.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBNET80211_RAW_TX_RATE_CONFIG">_oracles/libnet80211.a sha256 92550813de20ed0d51110dbd72b646e891a86a8a2f81fa53714ebf2ebf9c8f40; complete ieee80211_api.o esp_wifi_config_80211_tx and ieee80211_output.o esp_wifi_80211_tx. The public configuration copies a 12-byte phymode/rate/ERSU/DCM record through ic_set_80211_tx_rate_config. Only the raw 802.11 submission path reads that record: for phymode six it selects the HE descriptor branch, copies the configured rate to descriptor+0x0c and copies DCM to descriptor+0x31 bit 7. This API is therefore not an oracle for ordinary STA data rate-control packets unless a raw frame is explicitly submitted.</source>
      <source id="IEEE80211_HE_PHY_CAP_DCM">IEEE 802.11 HE PHY Capabilities byte three field semantics as exposed by Linux include/linux/ieee80211-he.h: bits 1:0 encode DCM maximum TX constellation and bits 4:3 encode DCM maximum RX constellation, with encodings NotSupported, BPSK, QPSK and 16-QAM.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_PP_HE_AMPDU_LENGTH">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_he.o ppCalTxHEAMPDULength size 0x3e2 and ppCalSubFrameLength size 0x3e. ppCalSubFrameLength rounds the low fourteen-bit DMA MPDU length, adds delimiter and empty-delimiter terms, then adds four when metadata byte seven bit zero is set. The final assembled A-MPDU byte count is stored at pTxRx[logical_queue]+0x44; complete mac_tx_set_hesig later shifts that exact value by eleven into HE_SU_SIGNAL_A2_LENGTH.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_PP_HE_SMPDU_LENGTH">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete pp_he.o ppCalTxHESMPDULength size 0x58 and ppCalSubFrameLength size 0x3e. ppCalTxHESMPDULength rounds the low-twenty-bit DMA metadata payload length to four bytes, calls ppCalDeliNum and ppCalSubFrameLength, sets descriptor byte 0x32 bit two, sets frame byte 0x26 to one and descriptor byte 0x2a to one. ppCalSubFrameLength computes round4(payload_length)+4*(metadata_byte4+1)+4*(metadata_byte7&amp;1). The live vendor raw frame supplies payload_length 28 for the 24-byte MPDU plus hardware FCS, metadata byte4 zero and byte7 zero, yielding the qualified 32-byte HE S-MPDU APEP.</source>
      <source id="ESP_WIFI_SYS_S31_HE_SU_SIG">Sibling esp-wifi-sys commit 72b97e6fe55307aa92c8c1edf3fdb3f4df816e80, c/headers/esp32s31/esp_private/esp_wifi_he_types_private.h complete esp_wifi_su_siga1_t and packed esp_wifi_su_siga2_t layouts. These standard field names are joined only to bit positions independently exercised by the complete S31 blob formatter.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_HE20_MCS9_SU_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/bin/wifi_sta.rs wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver and a nearby FRITZ!Box HE20 WPA2 BSS, 2026-07-29. The probe replaced pp_wdev_funcs callback slot 0xec, called the original formatter and synchronously copied all four queue-control words, 31 vector words and descriptor inputs before queue enable. Two MCS9 uplink A-MPDU captures returned descriptor rate 35 and flags 0xc0403009. APEP length 0x76 produced PLCP1 0x04083000, HE A1 0xfc205b4f or 0xfc605b4f as GI/LTF changed, HE A2/length 0x1003b105, power 0x05050505, counts 0x00004081 and length control 0x00400244. The subsequent vendor throughput path reported HE A1 0xfc205b4f and HE A2/length 0x1030d105, independently proving APEP length 0x061a. The public fixed-rate request value and live descriptor rate are both 35; certification-test value 0x29 belongs to a separate domain.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_HE20_MCS0_DCM_RAW_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/bin/wifi_sta.rs wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver and a controlled AX211 HE20 WPA2 BSS, 2026-07-29. After HE association, esp_wifi_config_80211_tx accepted phymode six, public rate 26/MCS0/GI800 and DCM true. A deliberately submitted 24-byte non-QoS raw data frame then traversed the only blob consumer of that configuration. Synchronous interposition captured descriptor flags 0xc0407008, rate 0x1a, PLCP0 0x01631630, PLCP1 0x0401a000, HE-SIG-A1 0xfc204087, HE-SIG-A2 0x00010105, power 0x05050505 and LENGTH_CONTROL 0x004002c4. Its DMA descriptor word 0xc0090040 encoded capacity 64 and used length 36; the buffer began with metadata 0x0100001c followed by a 24-byte MPDU and a four-byte hardware-FCS slot. The vendor completion callback subsequently reported rate 26 and status zero, qualifying ordinary ACK reception. This distinguishes explicit DCM from rcGetDCMMaxRate fallback codes 0x10/0x11/0x13.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE20_MCS0_DCM_SMPDU_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile with complete open PHY and MAC, controlled AX211 HE20 WPA2 AP on channel 11, 2026-07-29. After open scan, HE association, WPA2 and DHCP, the typed owner submitted one 24-byte non-QoS HE20 BCC DCM MCS0 S-MPDU using the exact bounded vendor DMA layout. Hardware completion returned status zero, proving ordinary ACK reception. The synchronous queue snapshot carried rate 0x1a, PLCP0 format one at 0x01636230 with only the live descriptor-address bits differing from vendor, PLCP1 0x0401a000, HE-SIG-A1 0xfc204087, HE-SIG-A2 0x00010105, power 0x14141314 and LENGTH_CONTROL 0x004002c4. The immediately following two-MPDU DCM A-MPDU retained status five and no BlockAck for all three supported GI/LTF profiles, localizing the remaining DCM failure to aggregate construction or BA handling rather than PHY, power, HE-SIG or DCM coding.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE20_MCS0_DCM_AMPDU_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile with complete open PHY and MAC, and a nearby OnePlus IN2023 Android-13 HE20 WPA2 SoftAP on channel 11, 2026-07-29. Android reported Ieee80211axEnabled=true; the association HE PHY capability advertised BPSK DCM receive, and the open path completed WPA2, protected RX and DHCP before the probe. A separate typed MCS0 DCM S-MPDU first received an ordinary ACK. The matrix then used valid minimum Ethernet bodies so the exact zero-TXOP ROM APEP table, blob DCM-halving branch and owned delimiter/MPDU/MIC/FCS accumulator admitted real multi-subframe aggregates: 30 MPDUs at 2xLTF/0.8 us, 29 at 2xLTF/1.6 us and 26 at 4xLTF/3.2 us. The first 30-MPDU aggregate completed with status zero, acknowledged all 30 sequence numbers and required one attempt. Twenty-seven complete bounded rounds, each containing 64 aggregates at every supported GI/LTF profile, reported zero failed profiles and zero terminal retry failures. This qualifies BPSK DCM S-MPDU and multi-subframe A-MPDU TX, APEP bounding, BlockAck and aggregate retry; the peer did not advertise QPSK or 16-QAM DCM receive, so MCS1 and MCS3 remain unqualified.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE20_MCS9_AMPDU_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust open-radio-phy-prelude-hil on ESP32-S31 rev0 and the same nearby FRITZ!Box HE20 WPA2 BSS, 2026-07-29. The fully open PHY/MAC path associated as HE20, installed the recovered HE peer state, then published selector-one GI/LTF, descriptor rate 0x23/MCS9 and 32 owned CCMP MPDUs through the typed HE queue program. The first aggregate completed with status zero and a full BlockAck bitmap 0x00000000ffffffff on its first attempt. A sustained raw-MAC run exceeded 13,800 aggregates with tx_ampdu_partial zero, RX dropped zero and five-second Ethernet-payload windows of 83.6 to 87.5 Mbit/s. This qualifies the complete bounded HE SU q0 image and its ordered PAC publication, not OFDMA, DCM, LDPC, STBC or beamforming.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE20_STBC_NSTS_2026_07_30">../esp32s31_rust firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, fully open PHY/MAC against the nearby FRITZ!Box HE20 WPA2 BSS, 2026-07-30. During a controlled 10-Mbit/s UDP downlink the RX owner captured HE-SIG-A1 0x00e0591b and HE-SIG-A2 0x4a0c for HE-SU MCS3, and later 0x00a0594b/0x520c for MCS9. Both vectors set STBC and encode bits 25:23 as one. Because the S31 is 1T1R, this is two space-time streams generated from one spatial stream and independently disproves the previous unconditional spatial_streams_minus_one label.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HE20_MCS9_EMPTY_DELIMITERS_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust open-radio-phy-prelude-hil on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled AX211 HE20 WPA2 AP on channel 11, 2026-07-29. A deterministic 32-MPDU protected-QoS aggregate used 54-byte PSDUs, HE20 MCS9, 2xLTF/0.8-us GI and an explicit 16-us density. Complete blob arithmetic produced minimum subframe length 230, 43 empty four-byte delimiters after every non-final MPDU and APEP length 7250. Keeping the old fixed queue PROTECTION value 0x31 produced completion status four and zero acknowledged MPDUs after four attempts. Changing only all three PROTECTION lanes to 230 produced status zero, a first-attempt BlockAck bitmap 0x00000000ffffffff and then more than 13,000 acknowledged MPDUs without final retry failure. This A/B HIL qualifies metadata-byte-four delimiter generation, final-tail APEP accounting and the descriptor-offset-0x28 to PROTECTION-lane mapping together.</source>
      <source id="BLOB_LIBPP_TRC_AMPDU_PARAM">_oracles/libpp.a sha256 f863c65c3ed89cf5d2a2cbe0d6bca3b783ca35788a704bb68e13958e4b94958e; complete trc.o rcUpdateAMPDUParam body, size 0xde. For non-HE HT peer types it maps HT A-MPDU Parameters bits 1:0, the maximum-length exponent, to byte ceilings 0x1fff, 0x3fff, 0x7fff and 0xffff, and maps minimum MPDU start-spacing code 0..4,5,6,7 to finite hardware values 20,40,76,148 stored at peer-state offset 0x82. Complete pp.o ppCheckTxAMPDUlength compares the accumulated aggregate against that peer byte ceiling. Complete hal_mac_tx.o mac_tx_set_htsig, size 0x23c, reads the spacing halfword and copies it into bits 9:0, 19:10 and 29:20 of the ordinary queue PROTECTION word through three fresh-read RMW edges.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_ACTIVE_HT_VECTOR_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust firmware wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver and a controlled Linux WPA2 HT20 AP, 2026-07-29. The probe polled all four queue owners and copied the complete 31-word vector plus four control words before logging only while PLCP0 format two was hardware-owned. The coherent HT queue contained PROTECTION=0x0280a028 and HT_DESCRIPTOR_COUNTS=0x00004081. The former is exactly three copies of negotiated spacing value 40; the latter is three copies of descriptor count one. This distinguishes the two physical registers and HIL-qualifies the complete blob field mapping.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_HT20_MCS0_SINGLE_PPDU_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/bin/wifi_sta.rs wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver and a controlled Linux WPA2 HT20 AP, 2026-07-29. After connection the probe replaced pp_wdev_funcs callback slot 0xec, called the original executable SRAM formatter thunk and copied the queue image synchronously before returning. Complete ROM lmacSetTxFrame at 0x2f835590..0x2f8355ae reaches that callback; complete ROM hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu is at 0x2f8352bc. A fixed-rate MCS0 non-A-MPDU frame of length 0x6e returned descriptor flags 0x00003009, PLCP0 control 0x016312fc before ownership publication, PLCP1 0x02090000, HT_SIGNAL 0x07006e00, DATA_LENGTH 0x0000006e, LENGTH_CONTROL 0x000002c4, HT_DESCRIPTOR_COUNTS 0x00004081 and PROTECTION 0x0280a028. This exact synchronous single-MPDU image distinguishes PLCP format one and entry class zero from the earlier active MCS7 A-MPDU image, which used format two and entry class one.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_HT_AMPDU_PPDU">Earlier ESP32-S31 complete-vendor HIL final-link wrappers around ppAssembleAMPDU and hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu, retained in docs/esp32s31-async-boundaries.md. A two-MPDU HT20 MCS7/SGI chain had aggregate length 0x0c2e, QoS sequences 0x014/0x015, first descriptor flags 0x004c2009 after assembly, PLCP format two, HT_SIGNAL 0x8f0c2e07, DATA_LENGTH 0x70400c2e and LENGTH_CONTROL 0x00400244. A separate six-MPDU capture proved aggregate byte accounting and descriptor-count publication. The oracle-only vendor/RTOS run reached about 53.4 Mbit/s UDP; this source qualifies the finite aggregate formatter and topology, not the current open-driver throughput.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HT_AMPDU_DIRECT_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile with ISR and DMA audited in internal SRAM, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled Linux WPA2 AP on channel 11 HT40-, 2026-07-29. The Rust STA initiated a TID-0 immediate BlockAck agreement with window four, retained separate pinned storage for single and aggregate submission, and transmitted four observed two-MPDU A-MPDUs at HT40 MCS7 SGI. Every completion reported both submitted sequence bits through a BlockAck bitmap ending in 0x000f, with zero aggregate hardware timeouts. The same run continued using the single-MPDU path whenever only one network frame was queued. This qualifies the open direct-DMA descriptor head, PLCP format two, aggregate HT-SIG/length class, descriptor-count two and BlockAck-before-completion-clear ordering; it does not yet qualify partial-BlockAck retry or a throughput ceiling.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HT_AMPDU_32_RETRY_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile with ISR and DMA audited in internal SRAM, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled Linux WPA2 AP on channel 11 HT40-, 2026-07-29. The peer HT A-MPDU parameter byte was 0x17, maximum-length exponent three. Applying the complete rcUpdateAMPDUParam mapping allowed the open owner to submit 32 full-size MPDUs totaling 48,448 aggregate bytes; the first completion returned starting sequence 2717 and bitmap 0x00000000ffffffff. PTI remained 0x00111110, proving its count one is independent of the 32 values in HT_DESCRIPTOR_COUNTS. Replacing individual missing-MPDU retries with the ppResortTxAMPDU-compatible retained retry aggregate reduced partial original submissions from 352/1044 to 50/2748 and raised HT40 MCS7 LGI UDP enqueue throughput from 38-41 to 49.6-55.2 Mbit/s. HT40 MCS7 SGI then produced 53.1-59.3 Mbit/s and Linux independently reported RX bitrate 150.0 Mbit/s MCS7 40MHz short GI. No aggregate hardware timeout occurred.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HT_AMPDU_RAW_CADENCE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled Linux WPA2 AP on channel 11 HT40-, 2026-07-29. A raw protected-QoS profile retained real CCMP, Sequence Control, DMA, 30-MPDU A-MPDU and BlockAck handling but removed Embassy UDP/IP production. It delivered 63.6-76.8 Mbit/s of 1472-byte Ethernet payload at MCS7 40MHz short GI. Across 3811 original aggregates, cadence averaged 5194 us per original and 3201 us from each hardware-submit edge to completion; 5087 aggregate attempts give 1.335 attempts per original. This matches the separately retained vendor direct-TX range 59.3-75.5 Mbit/s and localizes the remaining 100-Mbit/s gap to serialized preparation/completion plus missing-BlockAck retries rather than the former 21-MPDU byte ceiling.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_HT_SINGLE_EXTREMES_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, standard psram-code-psram-data profile with ISR and DMA audited in internal SRAM, complete open PHY and MAC, controlled Linux WPA2 AP on channel 11. HT20 MCS0 LGI completed first-attempt Authentication, Association, WPA2 and DHCP; 200/200 ICMP replies completed at 2.483-ms average RTT, while the open TX counters recorded 210 immediate successes, two recovered ACK retries, zero other failures and zero hardware timeouts over 212 attempts. HT40 MCS7 SGI then negotiated 150 Mbit/s in both directions; 500/500 ICMP replies completed at 2.203-ms average RTT, while open TX recorded 510 immediate successes and two recovered ACK retries over 512 attempts. These are single-MPDU results. They hardware-qualify PLCP format one and both extreme MCS/CBW/GI encodings; they do not qualify the separate A-MPDU constructor.</source>
      <source id="MIGRATION_LMAC_TX">Git parent of migration-promotion commit f233006, migration/esp32s31-hybrid-runtime/src/lmac.rs; exact ESP32-S31 queue-bank address/stride transcription and async timeout/completion path later promoted into driver/esp32s31/wifi/lmac/src/tx.rs. Existing open authentication and connected-network HIL qualify the ordinary queue-zero path.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_RX_LIVE_APPEND_2026_07_27">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs run_connected_network on ESP32-S31 rev0, psram-code-psram-data profile, 2026-07-27; rotating 32-entry ring survived more than 7000 receives and completed open scan, WPA2, DHCP and 5/5 ICMP echo with zero loss</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_MAC_IRQ_STATUS_CLASSIFICATION_2026_08_03">hil/esp32s31/runtime open-radio connected RX classification on ESP32-S31 rev0, 2026-08-03, documented in docs/hil/2026-08-02-esp32s31-pinned-rx-throughput.md; a sustained 30-second HE20 RX run recorded 220732 RX-bearing first STATUS snapshots with auxiliary bits 5 and 24, no spurious first snapshot and no bounded acknowledgement-loop saturation</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_AUTH_PLCP_FORMAT_2026_07_28">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on connected ESP32-S31 rev0, open PHY and MAC, 2026-07-28. Controlled A/B kept the 30-byte authentication MPDU, descriptor, PLCP1 0x22, power, rate, channel and RX policy fixed. Format one yielded completion status five with no response; format zero yielded status zero and one addressed authentication response, but later format-zero repetitions failed. Earlier repeated format-one runs had completed authentication through DHCP. Therefore this experiment proves that TX completion status is not by itself a protocol-success oracle; it does not supersede the instruction-exact mac_tx_set_plcp0 mapping.</source>
      <source id="HIL_VENDOR_STA_AUTH_POLICY_2026_07_28">../esp32s31_rust firmware wifi-sta-auth-probe on ESP32-S31 rev0 with the complete vendor driver, 2026-07-28. The first Open Authentication TX capture showed queue-zero RX filter 0x0001c387. This exactly matches wifi_set_rx_policy jump-table case six, including UBSSID-policy bits 8 and 1 set; the vendor station then associated, completed WPA2 and obtained DHCP. Applying only these two bits to the open driver reproduced the register image but did not independently cure its intermittent TX status-five/authentication timeout.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_TX_POWER_CONNECTIVITY_2026_07_28">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, psram-code-psram-data, open PHY and MAC, 2026-07-28. With the HIL API limit 80 quarter-dBm and resulting ordinary queue power code 20, three consecutive reset-to-network runs completed Authentication and Association on their first MAC attempts, WPA2 and DHCP. A host test then received 200 of 200 ICMP replies with 4.613 ms average RTT; the device observed four raw ACK timeouts among 215 attempts and recovered all four by retrying the same encoded MPDU. With limit 20 quarter-dBm and resulting code 5, repeated runs included complete twelve-attempt Authentication failures. This is connectivity evidence for the current open profile, not proof that the open and vendor power/gain-table encodings are equivalent; the complete vendor driver also succeeds with queue code 5, so that mismatch remains localized for investigation.</source>
      <source id="HIL_OPEN_LEGACY_RTS_RATE_2026_07_29">../esp32s31_rust/firmware/esp32s31/app/src/open_radio_phy_prelude_hil.rs on ESP32-S31 rev0, psram-code-psram-data, open PHY and MAC, controlled Linux WPA2 AP on channel 11 HT40-, 2026-07-29. Before the vendor basic-rate mapping, fixed 54-Mbit/s data with LENGTH_CONTROL incorrectly carrying rate 54 lost 25 to 39 percent of ICMP samples. Fixed 6M and 24M each completed 200/200, while 48M completed 199/200. After restoring complete mac_tx_get_rts_rate semantics so 54M publishes basic rate 24M and derives RTS power separately, 54M completed 197/200 followed by 495/500, with 1.975-ms and 2.353-ms average RTT. Linux reported the station RX bitrate as 54.0 Mbit/s, five AP-side TX retries and one AP-side TX failure over 709 packets. This qualifies the rate-dependent LENGTH_CONTROL field and strongly localizes the former loss to the wrong basic-rate image.</source>
